Found during k106. Two leftovers of the k106 window:
1. Streamable HTTP: a call whose start_p resolved (upstream ready) but whose send runs after a stop with no start after it goes out with no Mcp-Session-Id -- the stop already ended the session, a stateful remote answers 400 -- and is counted on no session. Options: fail it as stopped, or treat it as a call on a stopped upstream and start it (lazy start). Decide which.
2. HTTP+SSE: the same kind of call (and one that comes upon a start under way) fails at once with "upstream NAME: not connected" (k90) instead of waiting for the start as Streamable HTTP now does (k106). Make SSE consistent once 1 is decided.

Decision by the main session (2026-11-10), under the maintainer's 'erledige die tickets von karr'; the maintainer may veto: 1: a call let through just before a stop is a call on a stopped upstream and starts it (lazy start), so it goes out on a session. 2: HTTP+SSE then waits for a start under way, as Streamable HTTP does since k106.

Committed as afc2cbc (Start an HTTP upstream again for a call let through just before a stop, over SSE too).
